<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">French protectorate of Annam</h1><p class="st-meta">1883 CE – 1945 CE · capital Hue</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Central Vietnam under French protection from 1883, where the Nguyen emperors kept their court at Hue but real power lay with the French résident.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the French captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> and the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tu-duc">Emperor Tu Duc</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1883">Harmand Treaty</a> of 1883 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1884">Patenotre Treaty</a> of 1884 forced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty">Nguyen dynasty</a> to accept French protection. The central region, which Vietnamese called Trung Ky, became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-general-to-pacify-the-south">Annam</a>, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-tonkin">Tonkin</a> was placed under separate arrangements.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The emperors at Hue kept their palaces, mandarins and Confucian rituals, but a French résident supérieur controlled policy, taxes and appointments. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> deposed emperors who resisted, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ham-nghi">Ham Nghi</a>, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/can-vuong">Can Vuong movement</a> from 1885, and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanh-thai">Thanh Thai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duy-tan">Duy Tan</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-general-to-pacify-the-south">Annam</a> was poorer than <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-cochinchina">Cochinchina</a>, with coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> farming and highland plantations.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-general-to-pacify-the-south">Annam</a> was part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-indochina">French Indochina</a> from 1887. In March 1945 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> ended French rule, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/empire-of-vietnam">Empire of Vietnam</a>. After his abdication to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> in August 1945 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> ceased to exist.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-protectorate-of-annam.jpg" alt="French protectorate of Annam" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: noUSERname · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Colonial_Annam.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1883 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hue</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dong Khanh, Khai Dinh, Bao Dai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Confucianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Annam, Protectorate of Annam, Trung Kỳ</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-annam" aria-label="French protectorate of Annam on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7610 1566 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French protectorate of Annam lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7930 1822L7930 1822M7930 1822L5054 728M7930 1822L7939 2031M7930 1822L7955 1898"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7930 1822h0M5054 728h0M7939 2031h0M7955 1898h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7930 1822h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7930 1822h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Hue. <a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-annam">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
